 Actionable methodology + copy-paste recipes for debugging Unix / Python / PyTorch programs. Apply the general loop first; then jump to the domain cheatsheet for the failure at hand. For scaling this up to large-model training/inference on real clusters (compute/storage/network, SLURM, throughput/memory, instabilities, fault tolerance, inference), pair this with [Machine Learning Engineering](https://github.com/stas00/ml-engineering/blob/master/SKILL.md).

+## Pixi-only setup
+
+Use Pixi for every debugging dependency. Inspect `pixi.toml` and its declared
+channels first; prefer conda packages from those channels, normally conda-forge.
+
+- Run tools already in the workspace with `pixi run`.
+- Use `pixi exec` for one-off diagnostic tools.
+- Add recurring tools with `pixi add`.
+- Use `pixi add --pypi` when a package is unavailable from the declared conda channels.
+- Enter an interactive environment with `pixi shell -e <environment>`.
+- Apply this setup policy to commands in the linked chapters.
+
+Setup is complete when each command runs through Pixi and recurring tools are
+recorded in `pixi.toml` and `pixi.lock`.
+
 ## The debugging loop

 The single most important idea: **most of the effort is in *locating* the cause; once you truly understand it, the fix is usually easy.** Optimize everything for reaching understanding faster.
